{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795302463,"nonce":"/Lwrei8QqKCtuSJDer+b7dffcmI=","message":"More evidence on the fixed floor with deep stacks. Lua official/cstack.lua passes in 0.13 s alone with a 1 MB floor. When four runs overlap at that floor, all four hang for over 50 s, with the pool-style default floor they finish in 0.5 s. One collection took 14 s to mark 319 KB. A loaded machine delays tier-up, so the interpreted recursion builds a huge stack, and every 1 MB of allocation scans all of it. The cost of a collection follows the stack depth and the floor ignores it. It happens with plain Immix and does not need the threads flag.","files":null}]}